Subject: [PATCH] mega_moe: single kernel takes any experts per rank and top-k, and a fused shared-expert slot

- small_m_eligible: admit 1..64 experts per rank (the planning pass uses one lane per local expert) and top-1..8,
  instead of only 384 experts / top-6. The DeepSeek-V4.1 DSpark draft MoE (128 experts, top-3) and the
  fused-shared-expert layout (392 experts, top-7) now take the single kernel.
- _use_direct_fixed_slot was the only place hard-wired to 48 experts per rank; every other stage (plan scan,
  route encoding, combine buffers and loops, LDS / dispatch-table sizes, config choice, 32-bit buffer offsets)
  was already generic.
- SmallMRuntime(shared_experts=N): the last N local slots of every rank are fused shared experts. They receive
  every local token, so they are excluded from the hot-expert test and the FP8-combine-row decision (otherwise
  every call switches to FP8 rows: FP32-reference error 0.0025 -> 0.0265), but still count toward the
  cached-weight decision.

Base: amd-aiter 0.1.29 + 0001-aiter-0.1.29-mega_moe-small_m-dsv41-flash.patch.
---
